---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import SocialMeta from "../components/SocialMeta.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Privacy Policy — Nail Bite Beaver</title>
    <SocialMeta
      title="Privacy Policy — Nail Bite Beaver"
      description="Nail Bite Beaver processes camera frames on your Mac only. No images are stored or uploaded. Learn what data stays local, and what license and update checks send."
      path="/privacy"
    />

    <!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
    <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-DM7ZR8WCHR"
    ></script>
    <script is:inline>
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      function gtag() {
        dataLayer.push(arguments);
      }
      gtag("js", new Date());
      gtag("config", "G-DM7ZR8WCHR");

      /**
       * Fire a custom GA4 event.
       * @param {string} eventName
       * @param {Record<string, string | number | boolean>} [params]
       */
      function trackEvent(eventName, params) {
        gtag("event", eventName, params);
      }
    </script>

    <style>
      @import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:wght@500;600;700;800&display=swap");

      html,
      body {
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }

      body {
        background: #f6ebda;
        color: #2c3e50;
        font-family: "Nunito", system-ui, sans-serif;
        font-weight: 500;
        margin: 0;
      }

      h1,
      h2,
      h3,
      strong {
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      a {
        color: #2c3e50;
      }

      a:hover,
      a:focus-visible {
        color: #c1763d;
      }

      .page {
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
      }

      .back-bar {
        position: fixed;
        top: 0;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        z-index: 10;
        background: #f6ebda;
      }

      .back-bar__inner {
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      }

      .back-link {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-underline-offset: 4px;
      }

      .page h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      .updated {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        color: #5a6b7a;
      }

      .tldr {
        margin: 2rem 0 0;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem;
        border-radius: 12px;
        background: rgba(193, 118, 61, 0.12);
        border: 1px solid rgba(193, 118, 61, 0.35);
      }

      .tldr__label {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #c1763d;
      }

      .tldr p {
        margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: #2c3e50;
      }

      .policy-section {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
      }

      .policy-section h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }

      .policy-section p,
      .policy-section li {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color: #5a6b7a;
      }

      .policy-section p {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
      }

      .policy-section ul {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
      }

      .policy-section li + li {
        margin-top: 0.45rem;
      }

      .policy-section a {
        font-weight: 700;
        text-underline-offset: 4px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="back-bar">
      <div class="back-bar__inner">
        <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to home</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <main class="page">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 30, 2026</p>

      <aside class="tldr">
        <p class="tldr__label">TL;DR</p>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver does not track you, does not collect analytics, and
          does not sell your data. Camera frames are processed entirely on your
          Mac to detect nail-biting and hand-to-face movement. No images or
          video are saved to disk or sent to us. The only network requests are
          for license validation (Lemon Squeezy) and update checks (Sparkle on
          direct downloads).
        </p>
      </aside>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. Data We Do Not Collect</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver does not collect, transmit, or store any of the
          following:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Personal information (name, email, address)</li>
          <li>Usage analytics or telemetry</li>
          <li>Camera images, video, or detection frames</li>
          <li>Crash reports</li>
          <li>Location data</li>
          <li>Browsing or app usage history</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          There are no analytics SDKs, no tracking pixels, and no third-party
          data collection of any kind embedded in the Nail Bite Beaver app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. On-Device Processing</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver uses your Mac’s camera to watch for nail-biting or
          hand-to-face movement. Detection runs entirely on your device with
          Apple’s Vision framework and a bundled on-device Core ML model.
        </p>
        <p>
          Camera frames are processed in memory only. A few short preview frames
          may appear briefly in the on-screen overlay when the beaver catches
          you — then they are discarded. This data never leaves your Mac and is
          not written to disk.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Local Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver stores a small amount of data locally on your Mac:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Preferences</strong> — Things like whether you have finished
            onboarding, kept in macOS UserDefaults.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Lifecycle logs</strong> — Simple text timestamps used to
            understand clean exits and recover from interrupted launches. These
            stay in the app’s Application Support folder and are never uploaded.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>No photos, video, or camera frames are saved.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Network Requests</h2>
        <p>Nail Bite Beaver makes exactly two types of network requests:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>License validation</strong> — When you activate your license
            key, Nail Bite Beaver sends your license key (and an instance name
            such as your Mac’s hostname) to Lemon Squeezy’s API for activation
            and periodic revalidation. Camera data and detection results are
            never included.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Update checks</strong> — Direct downloads use Sparkle, a
            standard open-source macOS update framework, to check for new
            versions from our update feed. This may send your macOS version and
            app version. App Store builds do not use Sparkle.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>That’s it. No other network requests are made by the app.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. Hardware Access</h2>
        <p>Nail Bite Beaver accesses the following on your Mac:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Camera</strong> — To detect nail-biting and hand-to-face
            movement on-device. macOS will prompt you for camera permission the
            first time. No video is recorded and no frames are uploaded.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver does <strong>not</strong> access your microphone,
          location, contacts, photos library, calendar, Bluetooth, USB devices,
          or accessibility features.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Lemon Squeezy</strong> — Payment processing and license key
            management. Purchases and refunds are handled by Lemon Squeezy. See
            <a
              href="https://www.lemonsqueezy.com/privacy"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer">Lemon Squeezy’s privacy policy</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Sparkle</strong> — Open-source update framework used by
            direct downloads. No data is shared with third parties through
            Sparkle beyond what is needed to check for and download updates from
            our own feed.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>7. Camera &amp; Detection in Detail</h2>
        <p>Here’s exactly what happens with camera data:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Processed on your Mac only.</strong> Face landmarks, hand
            pose, and object detection run locally. Nothing is sent to a remote
            model or server for analysis.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Not stored.</strong> Frames are not written to disk, not
            added to Photos, and not backed up by the app.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Never sent to us.</strong> There is no upload path for
            camera frames, screenshots, or detection results.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>No biometric profiling.</strong> Nail Bite Beaver does not
            build an identity profile, run face recognition against a database,
            or share biometric templates. Vision runs only to spot nail-biting /
            hand-to-face behavior in the moment.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>You control access.</strong> Revoke camera permission anytime
            in System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Camera. Without
            permission, monitoring cannot run.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver does not knowingly collect personal information from
          children. The app is not directed at children under 13, and camera
          detection data stays on-device.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be reflected
          on this page with an updated date. Continued use of Nail Bite Beaver
          after changes constitutes acceptance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy? Reach out at{" "}
          <a href="mailto:support@nailbitebeaver.com"
            >support@nailbitebeaver.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />

    <script is:inline>
      document.querySelector(".back-link")?.addEventListener("click", () => {
        trackEvent("privacy_back_click");
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
